## Quickstart

Once this module is generated, it can run an example from the generated module by:

```console
$ dagger call container-echo --string-arg=hello stdout
hello
```

## The project structure

The module is just a regular Elixir application. The structure looks like:

```text
.
├── dagger_sdk
├── lib
│   └── {{ .ModulePackage }}.ex
├── mix.exs
└── README.md
```

`lib` is the Elixir source code, and `{{ .ModulePackage }}.ex` is the main Dagger module.

`dagger_sdk` is written by `dagger generate`: it holds the Dagger Elixir SDK together with
the API bindings generated from your engine's schema. Commit it — the module runtime builds
from it and does not regenerate it.
